WEBVTT

00:07.549 --> 00:10.552
[dishes rattling]

00:11.762 --> 00:13.639
[Heeju] I wanted to run away
from the pawn shop.

00:14.765 --> 00:18.185
But there was a shadow of misfortune
that fell on my shoulders.

00:18.268 --> 00:21.688
It was a weight
that I just couldn't shake off.

00:23.899 --> 00:24.983
[gasps]

00:25.067 --> 00:28.070
[flies buzzing]

00:29.404 --> 00:30.781
[creaking]

00:30.864 --> 00:33.033
[inhales and exhales sharply]

00:35.869 --> 00:38.455
[Cheoljung] Do you know
how worried I've been?

00:38.539 --> 00:40.123
You've got a perfectly good home.

00:40.207 --> 00:41.583
Why are you putting yourself through this?

00:41.667 --> 00:44.461
Oh, no! Mm!

00:44.545 --> 00:46.213
[Cheoljung] Look at you.
Your poor hands.

00:46.296 --> 00:49.132
Whatever. Can you just go now?

00:50.050 --> 00:51.843
[exhales]

00:51.927 --> 00:53.387
'Kay, I'll go.

00:53.470 --> 00:55.430
[Cheoljung] But you should
come home more often.

00:56.390 --> 00:58.850
We can all have dinner together, yeah?

01:02.521 --> 01:04.356
[inhales on cigarette]

01:07.401 --> 01:09.444
Gross. That bastard.

01:14.324 --> 01:18.704
[Heeju] I swore to myself I would never
be lured by that light that got my mother.

01:19.871 --> 01:21.915
I needed a light of my own.

01:21.999 --> 01:23.792
One that would hide me from my shadow.

01:25.127 --> 01:28.589
But without money,
you don't have a lot of options.

01:31.842 --> 01:32.759
[roulette wheel rattling]

01:32.843 --> 01:35.846
[Heeju] Gold Land makes promises
of dazzling fortune.

01:35.929 --> 01:37.764
But that's not what I dreamed of.

01:39.016 --> 01:44.479
Maybe all I wanted was just some guarantee
that I could be safe here.

01:45.397 --> 01:47.357
It was all someone like me could hope for.

01:47.441 --> 01:49.151
[indistinct chatter]

01:54.197 --> 01:56.992
[chips clinking]

01:57.075 --> 01:58.243
[Male Gambler] Hey, hey, hey, hey.

01:58.327 --> 02:01.079
-What's the deal with these red ones?
-[Heeju] Sorry?

02:01.163 --> 02:03.623
They're all supposed to be yellow.
I exchanged them for yellow!

02:05.375 --> 02:06.376
Ch-change it!

02:07.794 --> 02:09.629
Hey! Hear me or what?

02:09.713 --> 02:11.423
-[Guard A] All right, that's enough.
-Do you think I'm stupid, bitch?

02:11.506 --> 02:13.717
-[Guard A] Time to go, sir.
-[Guard B] Let's go.

02:13.800 --> 02:15.719
[Male Gambler] Let go of me!
Get your hands off me!

02:15.802 --> 02:18.972
-Call the manager! Call the manager now!
-[Guard A] Get him out. Let's go!

02:19.056 --> 02:20.307
[Dokyung] What the hell?

02:20.974 --> 02:22.142
What's up with that guy?

02:26.438 --> 02:28.440
Oh.

02:28.523 --> 02:30.776
100 gold chips, please.

02:32.069 --> 02:34.571
[Heeju] That's when he walked
into my life.

02:34.655 --> 02:38.367
A man who seemed to be made
of nothing but good luck.

02:38.450 --> 02:41.953
He was like a mirage
that came out of nowhere.

02:42.037 --> 02:43.705
Something that didn't belong in my world.

02:44.623 --> 02:46.792
As if he'd disappear if I touched him.

02:48.126 --> 02:51.672
Time to see if luck is on
my side today.

02:53.965 --> 02:55.300
[Dokyung] Thank you, Miss Heeju.
STYLE
::cue()

03:05.018 --> 03:07.354
[Dokyung] I bought this on my way back
from Hong Kong. It's for you.

03:08.355 --> 03:09.898
Heard you like planes, so...

03:13.110 --> 03:16.738
Uh, 100 gold chips, please.

03:21.618 --> 03:22.911
[machine rattling]

03:31.503 --> 03:32.921
[Dokyung exhales sharply]

03:34.714 --> 03:37.801
Time to see if luck is on my side today.

03:41.346 --> 03:42.556
Thank you.

03:51.815 --> 03:53.400
[Dokyung exhaling]

03:53.483 --> 03:54.901
[Dokyung] Whew!

03:54.985 --> 03:57.571
[all gasping and laughing]

04:00.824 --> 04:01.867
[woman gasps]

04:01.950 --> 04:02.868
Yes!

04:02.951 --> 04:04.453
[crowd cheering]

04:04.536 --> 04:06.204
[applause]

04:09.332 --> 04:10.667
[Woman] Did you see that?

04:10.750 --> 04:14.421
[Dokyung breathing heavily]

04:15.797 --> 04:19.301
Hey, see this?
It's yours Heeju.

04:20.427 --> 04:22.053
I only won it because of you.

04:22.137 --> 04:23.388
[scoffs]

04:30.061 --> 04:31.521
[exhales]

04:32.939 --> 04:33.940
Uh...

04:34.900 --> 04:38.612
[indistinct chatter]

04:47.704 --> 04:49.164
[Cheoljung inhales deeply]

04:49.247 --> 04:52.334
Give me some gold chips,
why don't ya?

04:54.628 --> 04:57.464
This is where you were hiding, huh?

04:58.507 --> 05:00.967
[Cheoljung] Do you have any idea
how long I've been looking for you?

05:03.553 --> 05:05.096
[Heeju] Get out.

05:05.180 --> 05:07.140
I don't have anything to say to you.

05:07.224 --> 05:08.850
That's no way to talk to your uncle.

05:08.934 --> 05:12.687
Like it or not,
the two of us are family, ya know.

05:12.771 --> 05:14.272
You are not my family.

05:15.398 --> 05:17.400
Hmm.

05:18.151 --> 05:20.195
But you're my sweet little niece.

05:21.112 --> 05:22.697
[hiccups and grunts]

05:22.781 --> 05:25.826
Enough of this.
Let's just go home now.

05:25.909 --> 05:28.537
Did my aunt tell you, then?
Where to find me?

05:28.620 --> 05:29.538
[Cheoljung] Of course.

05:29.621 --> 05:31.122
She was worried sick.

05:31.206 --> 05:33.250
[Cheoljung] You're her only niece.

05:33.333 --> 05:36.086
Come back home now, really.
Heeju.

05:36.169 --> 05:38.004
-[Cheoljung] Do you really think...
-Security, he's drunk.

05:38.088 --> 05:41.383
...you can live in Jeongsan
without me finding out about it?

05:41.466 --> 05:42.509
-[Guard A] Let's go, let's go.
-[Cheoljung] Come on.

05:42.592 --> 05:45.136
[Cheoljung] I'm this girl's uncle, okay?

05:45.220 --> 05:48.473
Ah, shitheads!
Get the hell off of me!

05:48.557 --> 05:50.183
[Cheoljung] She's my niece!
I'm telling you!

05:50.267 --> 05:52.018
-[Guard B] Come on!
-Be sure to eat well, okay?

05:52.936 --> 05:55.355
-[Cheoljung] You've lost weight, you know!
-[Heeju] Even the light of this place

05:55.438 --> 05:57.607
-couldn't conceal my shadow.
-[Cheoljung] I'll be back for you! Heeju!
STYLE
::cue()

05:57.691 --> 06:04.155
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

06:04.781 --> 06:06.867
[Heeju] How much longer could I endure?

06:08.076 --> 06:09.661
Like my mother...

06:10.662 --> 06:12.414
...I was already starting to wither.

06:14.791 --> 06:16.960
I felt like I couldn't go on much longer.

06:18.003 --> 06:19.462
I had to reach for it.

06:20.797 --> 06:23.800
Even if it was just
a mirage that would disappear.

06:23.884 --> 06:26.887
[♪ sad music]

06:33.059 --> 06:34.060
[door lock beeps]

06:35.228 --> 06:36.229
[door opens]

06:56.374 --> 06:57.375
Heeju.

07:06.551 --> 07:07.552
Here you go.

07:08.553 --> 07:10.972
I exchanged those chips you gave me
into cash for you.

07:11.514 --> 07:12.515
[inhales sharply]

07:14.100 --> 07:17.979
Uh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean it that way.

07:19.147 --> 07:20.398
What did you mean, then?

07:20.482 --> 07:25.445
Well, either way it was up to you
to decide whether to come here or not.

07:28.281 --> 07:30.325
[Dokyung] But take this at least.

07:30.408 --> 07:32.661
As a token of my appreciation.

07:33.620 --> 07:35.205
[grunts]

07:37.999 --> 07:39.793
[Heeju] This is everything I have.

07:39.876 --> 07:43.213
Take the money and place
a single bet for me.

07:44.339 --> 07:46.091
[Heeju] I've decided to trust you.

07:46.174 --> 07:47.676
And for once in my life...

07:48.385 --> 07:51.513
...take a gamble and see if my life
has any luck at all.

07:54.974 --> 07:58.603
[Female Dealer] The game at table two
will start in one minute.

07:58.687 --> 08:00.438
[Female Dealer] You have one minute
if you want to play.

08:01.523 --> 08:04.484
[crowd cheering]

08:04.567 --> 08:05.902
[Dokyung] Congrats, Heeju.
Good job.

08:05.985 --> 08:08.571
You won.
The pot is all yours.

08:10.323 --> 08:11.866
[chips rattling]

08:11.950 --> 08:13.326
[Heeju exhales]

08:13.410 --> 08:14.994
Wait a sec, Heeju.

08:15.078 --> 08:16.287
Just a sec.

08:18.123 --> 08:20.291
-[Heeju gasping]
-It's okay.

08:20.375 --> 08:23.128
-[Dokyung] It's okay.
-[Heeju] Wait. I don't...

08:23.211 --> 08:25.130
Let's place these ones on top.

08:25.213 --> 08:26.548
What?

08:28.717 --> 08:30.343
Trust me, Heeju.

08:33.388 --> 08:36.391
[♪ hopeful music]

08:40.895 --> 08:41.896
[Heeju exhales]

08:46.526 --> 08:48.194
[Dokyung exhales]

08:51.906 --> 08:53.533
[Heeju sighs]

08:56.244 --> 08:59.664
[crowd whispering]

09:02.042 --> 09:03.084
[both exhale]

09:03.168 --> 09:04.335
Ten.

09:06.755 --> 09:08.006
[Heeju exhales]

09:08.715 --> 09:10.216
[Dokyung] Okay.

09:11.092 --> 09:14.471
[cheers and applause]

09:14.554 --> 09:16.431
[Heeju gasps]

09:16.514 --> 09:18.725
Heeju! Heeju, you did it!

09:18.808 --> 09:20.643
You won it all!

09:22.353 --> 09:24.397
[Dokyung] Okay, these are yours.

09:24.481 --> 09:25.899
[Heeju gasps]

09:25.982 --> 09:27.525
This is enough, right?

09:27.609 --> 09:28.943
Congratulations.

09:30.445 --> 09:34.240
[Heeju] From then on,
for the first time in my life,

09:34.324 --> 09:36.993
it finally felt like there
was a light in my world.

09:38.369 --> 09:40.413
Like I was seeing the sun
for the first time

09:40.497 --> 09:42.457
after coming out of a dark tunnel.

09:43.333 --> 09:47.962
It was warm and everything around me
was crystal clear.

09:48.046 --> 09:49.005
-Come here.
-What?

09:49.089 --> 09:52.717
[Heeju] Every moment,
every day filled with gratitude.

09:52.801 --> 09:54.260
I was happy.

09:55.678 --> 09:58.139
What, you don't like mine?
What's not to like?

09:58.223 --> 10:01.684
[indistinct chatter]
STYLE
::cue()

10:08.608 --> 10:09.609
[Dokyung] What are you staring at?

10:13.404 --> 10:16.282
[Heeju] Am I really allowed
to live like this?

10:16.366 --> 10:17.492
[Dokyung] What does that mean?

10:19.494 --> 10:20.870
Just like this.

10:22.831 --> 10:24.165
Like other people.

10:25.375 --> 10:26.751
Happy and calm.

10:29.671 --> 10:31.840
You met me,
so you must be lucky.

10:33.049 --> 10:34.676
[chuckles]

10:34.759 --> 10:37.345
You're the first person
to ever say that to me.

10:38.596 --> 10:40.098
Ever since I was a kid,

10:40.181 --> 10:43.017
everyone always told me I
was an unlucky little brat.

10:44.394 --> 10:45.645
[Heeju] And it was kind of true.

10:46.729 --> 10:48.648
So none of this feels real.

10:49.607 --> 10:51.359
Being happy like this.

10:53.570 --> 10:54.612
Being with you.

10:54.696 --> 10:56.573
[inhales and exhales sharply]

10:58.616 --> 11:00.118
Isn't happiness meant for everyone?

11:00.201 --> 11:01.202
Mm.

11:02.245 --> 11:04.414
[Dokyung] You don't have
to worry about anything now.

11:05.331 --> 11:06.875
Just trust me and follow my lead.

11:07.709 --> 11:09.252
This is barely the beginning.

11:09.335 --> 11:11.254
[Dokyung] From this moment on...

11:12.380 --> 11:16.134
...I'm gonna show you exactly
how lucky you are.

11:18.803 --> 11:19.804
Santé?

11:22.140 --> 11:23.266
[exhales]

11:23.975 --> 11:24.893
Santé.

11:24.976 --> 11:26.561
[glasses clink]

11:34.527 --> 11:37.238
[distant seagulls cawing]

11:40.033 --> 11:42.243
[Heeju giggles]

11:44.913 --> 11:50.919
NO ENTRY

11:57.342 --> 12:00.345
[♪ suspenseful music]

12:29.666 --> 12:30.667
[grunts]

12:45.181 --> 12:46.474
[Heeju] Is this mine?

12:48.017 --> 12:49.018
No.

12:50.228 --> 12:52.105
Then is it Lee Dokyung's?

12:53.481 --> 12:54.857
Also no.

12:56.609 --> 12:58.069
I don't know whose it is.

12:59.195 --> 13:01.406
Maybe I don't wanna know.

13:02.323 --> 13:04.617
But if it doesn't belong
to anyone anyway,

13:04.701 --> 13:05.702
why shouldn't I take it?

13:07.537 --> 13:09.622
At least,
that's what I kept telling myself.

13:11.165 --> 13:13.209
You're just doing what Lee Dokyung
told you to do.

13:14.127 --> 13:15.962
You can't help it because you love him.

13:16.671 --> 13:18.006
That's what you think, right?

13:19.215 --> 13:21.759
Did I really love Lee Dokyung?

13:21.843 --> 13:24.804
Or was it that I just wanted to escape?

13:26.347 --> 13:27.890
Did it really matter?

13:30.351 --> 13:36.024
No, but now I have
to decide for myself.

13:36.774 --> 13:39.944
What does it really mean to be happy?

13:41.195 --> 13:43.740
[inhales and exhales sharply]

13:43.823 --> 13:46.826
[♪ sad piano music]

14:05.553 --> 14:08.556
[♪ music continues]
STYLE
::cue()

14:27.366 --> 14:28.910
EPISODE 4
HIM

14:28.993 --> 14:31.412
[Jinman] Stop bugging me about it, okay?

14:31.954 --> 14:33.122
I'll find it soon.

14:33.206 --> 14:34.457
[indistinct chatter]

14:34.540 --> 14:36.459
Yes, I know that.

14:36.542 --> 14:38.586
The chairman will be back next week?

14:38.669 --> 14:40.546
[Jinman] I'll get back
to you as soon as I can.

14:41.255 --> 14:42.340
Yeah.

14:42.423 --> 14:43.674
[exhales]

14:43.758 --> 14:45.760
[Jinman] Oh! Ah!

14:45.843 --> 14:47.762
Ah, fuck me.

14:47.845 --> 14:49.138
Seriously?

14:49.222 --> 14:52.225
[indistinct chatter]

15:00.149 --> 15:02.401
Ah, shit.

15:05.113 --> 15:06.823
[mouse wheel scrolling]

15:06.906 --> 15:08.366
Is that a woman?

15:27.468 --> 15:30.388
WITNESS STATEMENT RECORD
WITNESS PERSONAL INFORMATION

15:37.311 --> 15:38.729
[Male Detective] And your name?

15:40.565 --> 15:41.941
[Sunok] Yeo Sunok.

15:45.111 --> 15:46.112
[Male Detective exhales sharply]

15:46.195 --> 15:47.780
[Male Detective] Around what time
did this happen?

15:50.700 --> 15:51.784
Um...

15:52.702 --> 15:55.413
[Sunok] Last night.
Around 10:00.

15:55.496 --> 15:57.415
[Male Detective] Okay, around 10:00 p.m.

15:57.498 --> 15:58.624
Afternoon, sir.

15:58.708 --> 15:59.959
-Wait!
-Yeah?

16:00.543 --> 16:02.003
Well, that woman.

16:02.086 --> 16:03.838
[Jinman] What's her deal?

16:03.921 --> 16:04.881
Ah, her?

16:04.964 --> 16:06.465
She was booked this morning
at a local precinct,

16:06.549 --> 16:07.550
but they handed it over to us.

16:07.633 --> 16:10.428
She bashed her husband with a golf club.
He's in the hospital.

16:10.511 --> 16:11.804
Her husband reported it?

16:11.888 --> 16:14.265
No, she reported it herself.

16:14.348 --> 16:15.600
[Jinman] What about the husband?

16:15.683 --> 16:16.976
He wants to press charges.

16:17.059 --> 16:20.229
According to him, she-
she was after his pawnshop's money.

16:20.313 --> 16:23.107
-Says he has evidence.
-[Mija] Sunok!

16:23.191 --> 16:26.444
Sunok! What's going on here?
Is it true?

16:26.527 --> 16:28.487
-Well, I'll be going.
-[grunts]

16:28.571 --> 16:30.531
-You didn't really do it, did you?
-Hi, there.

16:30.615 --> 16:31.991
[Male Detective]
Are you a family member?

16:32.074 --> 16:34.327
No, but she's like a sister.

16:34.410 --> 16:35.620
How did you find out?

16:35.703 --> 16:36.787
What are you saying?

16:36.871 --> 16:39.040
You called me to come and get you.

16:41.334 --> 16:43.169
Can you make sure she leaves?

16:43.252 --> 16:45.213
Sunok, dammit,
that's not what should concern you.

16:45.296 --> 16:46.881
[Mija] You shouldn't be here.

16:48.049 --> 16:50.176
[Mija] Detective, this woman
is very sick.

16:50.259 --> 16:52.303
She has terminal cancer.

16:54.472 --> 16:57.058
[Mija] I mean, she should be in
the hospital, not in a place like this!

16:57.141 --> 16:59.477
[Male Detective] I understand, but I
still have to continue processing her.

17:00.394 --> 17:02.396
-Detective, please!
-Jeongsan-gun.

17:02.480 --> 17:05.358
-Sunok!
-Five, dash, 18 Bukju.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.776
Detective!

17:06.859 --> 17:09.862
SAMJEON JEWELRY DEPARTMENT STORE

17:10.821 --> 17:13.324
[Woogy] Ah, okay.
No, no, no, no.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.284
Excuse me.

17:17.745 --> 17:19.247
Yeah, sure thing.

17:19.330 --> 17:20.665
Thank you. Mm.

17:21.290 --> 17:22.541
[inhales sharply]

17:22.625 --> 17:26.295
We could have made preparations
if you had called ahead of time.

17:26.379 --> 17:27.421
[Male Store Owner] Sorry about that.

17:30.007 --> 17:32.260
But we'll buy the gold bar.
We'll have the cash ready soon.

17:32.343 --> 17:33.386
[Male Store Owner] Do you mind waiting
a little longer?

17:33.469 --> 17:34.345
Of course.

17:34.428 --> 17:35.888
[chuckles]

17:38.182 --> 17:39.850
[exhales]

17:43.521 --> 17:45.856
Uh, sir. Excuse me.

17:46.983 --> 17:49.402
This one here.
Can I buy this?

17:49.485 --> 17:51.529
Uh, would you like to look
at that one, too?

17:51.612 --> 17:53.614
-Heh, yeah.
-Sure. Just one minute.

18:00.871 --> 18:02.081
[Female Store Owner] You want it in cash?

18:02.164 --> 18:03.874
130 million?

18:03.958 --> 18:05.167
Yeah.

18:05.251 --> 18:06.711
[exhale sharply]

18:06.794 --> 18:08.170
If you can't do it, don't worry.

18:08.254 --> 18:09.589
-I'll go somewhere else.
-Oh, no, no, no, no.

18:09.672 --> 18:12.133
[chuckles nervously]
Wait just a minute.

18:13.050 --> 18:14.260
[exhales]

18:16.304 --> 18:18.472
[Female Customer] Honey, I want this one!

18:18.556 --> 18:20.433
-Isn't it beautiful?
-Really?

18:20.516 --> 18:22.143
You don't want this one?
It's shiny.

18:22.226 --> 18:23.728
Happy with that little thing?

18:23.811 --> 18:25.146
[chuckles]

18:25.980 --> 18:26.981
[grunts]

18:29.900 --> 18:31.902
[breathing heavily]

18:35.114 --> 18:36.365
You don't want to count to make sure?

18:36.449 --> 18:39.744
I plan on doing more business with you,
so I'm sure it's the right amount.

18:39.827 --> 18:41.287
Ah, yes.

18:41.370 --> 18:42.413
[inhales sharply]

18:42.496 --> 18:44.832
TRANSFEREE: KIM MINCHEOL

18:44.915 --> 18:46.584
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KIM MINCHEOL
STYLE
::cue()

18:46.667 --> 18:48.336
JEWELRY WORLD

18:48.419 --> 18:50.171
[cell phone vibrating]

18:50.254 --> 18:52.048
Heeju, what's up?

18:52.131 --> 18:53.132
[Heeju] Where are you?

18:54.050 --> 18:55.593
Where do you think? Daejeong.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.262
Just finishing up with the potatoes.

18:58.721 --> 18:59.722
Where are you?

18:59.805 --> 19:01.057
You don't need to know.

19:02.350 --> 19:04.560
I need you to just show me where you
are right now.

19:04.644 --> 19:06.979
[Woogy] Ah, why can't you just trust me?

19:09.231 --> 19:11.233
See? Jewelry stores.

19:12.610 --> 19:13.611
[Woogy] By the way,

19:13.694 --> 19:15.071
I think I'm gonna get a new car.

19:15.905 --> 19:17.782
[Woogy] I'm young and rich now.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.493
This car doesn't cut it anymore.
[car alarm beeps]

19:22.244 --> 19:23.287
[exhales sharply]

19:23.371 --> 19:26.582
[Woogy] Well anyway,
I'll be headed over there later.

19:26.666 --> 19:29.585
You just, uh, bring the gold.

19:30.211 --> 19:31.253
See you soon.

19:35.216 --> 19:36.217
[exhales sharply]

19:37.802 --> 19:40.680
[lightly chuckling]

19:44.809 --> 19:45.893
[car alarm beeps]

19:49.146 --> 19:52.149
[♪ suspenseful music]

19:56.237 --> 20:00.074
YANGPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

20:04.537 --> 20:06.205
[coughing]

20:10.126 --> 20:11.127
[car alarm beeps]

20:34.692 --> 20:35.693
[camera shutter clicks]

20:37.153 --> 20:38.154
[door opens]

20:39.155 --> 20:40.781
[camera shutter clicks]

20:40.865 --> 20:41.866
And who are you?

20:41.949 --> 20:45.661
Oh, uh, hi.
Jeongsan Police Department.

20:45.745 --> 20:48.622
Uh, Detective Kim Jinman.

20:48.706 --> 20:51.125
Here's my business card for you.

20:51.208 --> 20:52.918
[Yujin] The Jeongsan Police?

20:53.002 --> 20:55.713
I thought that my team was cleared
of any involvement

20:55.796 --> 20:57.339
and the investigation was over.

20:57.423 --> 20:59.300
Yeah, sort of.

20:59.383 --> 21:01.844
This particular case has become so complex

21:01.927 --> 21:04.138
that we're conducting
a joint investigation.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.432
And regarding Mr. Lee Dokyung,

21:06.515 --> 21:07.933
we haven't caught the suspect
for the hit-and-run.

21:09.810 --> 21:12.354
So the police still haven't been able
to find the casket?

21:12.438 --> 21:15.191
-No, not yet.
-[Yujin] Hmm.

21:15.274 --> 21:16.859
What do you want to ask me about, exactly?

21:17.985 --> 21:19.278
You're close with Lee Dokyung, right?

21:19.361 --> 21:20.613
You two call each other a lot?

21:21.697 --> 21:23.032
Because of work, I guess.

21:23.616 --> 21:25.785
There's nothing going on between us.

21:25.868 --> 21:27.453
[exhales sharply]

21:27.536 --> 21:29.288
It's been a while since we've talked.

21:30.456 --> 21:31.749
So what's going on?

21:32.416 --> 21:33.918
[inhales sharply]

21:34.001 --> 21:36.128
I don't really know,
but I might need a favor.

21:36.212 --> 21:37.880
[Yujin inhales on cigarette]

21:37.963 --> 21:40.132
Could you get something through customs
for me?

21:40.216 --> 21:42.259
[exhales]
Favor?

21:43.636 --> 21:44.887
Why?

21:44.970 --> 21:47.014
Why not just tell me you love me
like you used to?

21:48.224 --> 21:49.767
[Yujin] You can't say it anymore?

21:51.644 --> 21:53.938
You said it just fine
when you were cheating on me.

21:54.605 --> 21:57.608
This is important.
I'm not playing around here.

21:57.691 --> 22:00.528
[Jinman] You spoke with him on the phone
on the day of the accident, the fourth.

22:01.529 --> 22:02.613
[exhales sharply]

22:02.696 --> 22:05.491
Was I the only person who spoke
to Lee Dokyung that day?

22:05.574 --> 22:06.575
[Jinman] Not at all.

22:06.659 --> 22:08.661
Miss, this is just standard procedure.

22:08.744 --> 22:09.954
I have to ask, 'kay?

22:11.121 --> 22:12.623
Lee Dokyung, what did he say?

22:12.706 --> 22:13.833
FIRST OFFICER LEE DOKYUNG:

22:13.916 --> 22:15.709
THIS IS THE LAST TIME.
PLEASE JUST COME ONE MORE TIME TOMORROW.

22:15.793 --> 22:17.795
I CAN GIVE YOU WHAT YOU REALLY WANT.
NATIONAL ROUTE 6, 50-7

22:20.589 --> 22:22.466
[Yujin] We just talked
about personal stuff.

22:23.717 --> 22:25.928
But I don't really feel like getting
into all that right now.

22:26.011 --> 22:27.388
Oh.

22:28.556 --> 22:32.017
So you're close enough to speak
about personal matters on the phone. Mm.

22:32.101 --> 22:34.395
[Jinman] The day of the accident, then.

22:34.979 --> 22:37.356
Do you happen to know anyone who
could verify where you were?

22:38.274 --> 22:39.400
My alibi?

22:39.483 --> 22:41.068
Your alibi, yeah.

22:41.151 --> 22:42.570
You've already gone through
my call history.
STYLE
::cue()

22:42.653 --> 22:44.154
Shouldn't you already know?

22:44.238 --> 22:45.865
You see, the thing is,

22:45.948 --> 22:49.243
we can't verify anything you did after
the call with Lee Dokyung.

22:49.326 --> 22:52.413
At 10:00 p.m., you turned your phone off
for the rest of the night.

22:52.496 --> 22:55.332
[Yujin] Well, I would have been home
at that time.

22:55.416 --> 22:56.500
Mm-hmm.

22:57.626 --> 23:00.504
Ah, wait.
I went to the theater that night.

23:00.588 --> 23:02.381
For a late night movie.

23:02.464 --> 23:04.758
Movie theater?
Which theater did you go to?

23:04.842 --> 23:06.051
The theater in Sokcho.

23:06.135 --> 23:08.596
Alone or with someone?

23:09.513 --> 23:11.891
-I went alone.
-[Jinman] I see.

23:11.974 --> 23:14.351
[groaning]

23:14.435 --> 23:18.063
Do you happen to have anything that you
can show me like a ticket stub

23:18.147 --> 23:20.482
or reservation E-mail that shows you
were there that night?

23:21.442 --> 23:22.776
I'll be sure to look for it.

23:23.319 --> 23:25.321
[Jinman] Yes, please do.
I'd appreciate that.

23:26.947 --> 23:28.157
You know what?

23:29.074 --> 23:30.075
[Jinman chuckles]

23:30.159 --> 23:31.076
[Jinman] Whenever I question a suspect,

23:31.160 --> 23:34.705
the most common alibi
is that they were at the theater.

23:34.788 --> 23:36.498
If you had told me you were at home,

23:36.582 --> 23:39.293
I could have confirmed with
the surveillance cameras pretty easily.

23:39.752 --> 23:41.754
Unfortunately, the movie theaters
are trickier.

23:43.213 --> 23:45.299
[Jinman] Did you drive to the theater?

23:46.216 --> 23:48.093
-Well, no.
-[Jinman] Ah.

23:48.177 --> 23:49.887
[Dokyung] It's not a big deal.
It's honestly nothing.

23:49.970 --> 23:52.848
Just wait for my call and then bring
a van to the location I tell you.

23:52.932 --> 23:54.058
That's all.

23:54.892 --> 23:55.893
No.

23:55.976 --> 23:57.353
[exhales]

23:57.436 --> 23:58.812
Get out.

23:58.896 --> 24:00.064
Do it yourself.

24:00.147 --> 24:01.565
Don't even think about involving me.

24:01.649 --> 24:03.317
It's a billion.

24:03.400 --> 24:04.777
Is this what you meant
by giving me what I wanted?

24:04.860 --> 24:06.570
Yujin! Are you listening?

24:06.654 --> 24:08.614
Not a million.
It's a billion won.

24:08.697 --> 24:10.616
Don't you think that amount
is worth betting on?

24:10.699 --> 24:11.825
[Yujin] Betting?

24:11.909 --> 24:14.453
Your whole life is just one big gamble.

24:15.245 --> 24:16.497
No.

24:16.580 --> 24:19.708
[Yujin] It just never ends with you.
There will always be more.

24:19.792 --> 24:21.794
You'll keep doing this until it kills you.

24:23.003 --> 24:24.922
[Yujin] But you don't get to ruin my life,
too, so get out.

24:25.798 --> 24:28.676
[groans]
Yujin, we're so close. You can't-

24:28.759 --> 24:30.511
don't-don't tell me
you're bailing out now!

24:32.888 --> 24:34.640
[Yujin] Dokyung, this isn't fun anymore.

24:34.723 --> 24:37.309
-What?
-[Yujin] Get out.

24:38.978 --> 24:40.354
I said go.

24:43.232 --> 24:44.233
[exhales sharply]

24:45.359 --> 24:48.362
[car engine turns over]

24:52.700 --> 24:55.285
-Am I a suspect?
-[Jinman] Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

24:55.369 --> 24:59.164
I'm just saying, it's quite a coincidence,
the whole theater thing. Yeah.

24:59.248 --> 25:00.624
[Jinman] I get it, though.

25:03.836 --> 25:05.004
[Jinman] Hmm.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.549
So what's going to happen
to Lee Dokyung after all this?

25:08.632 --> 25:12.970
[Jinman] Ah, well, he'll be transferred
to a detention center upon recovery

25:13.053 --> 25:15.597
and then depending on
the outcome of his trial,

25:15.681 --> 25:18.517
I'd say he'll likely serve
a year or two in prison.

25:18.600 --> 25:20.978
I thought you told me you hadn't found
the casket yet.

25:21.061 --> 25:24.481
[Yujin] If there's no evidence,
will he still go to jail?

25:24.565 --> 25:26.859
No, but I'm sure we'll find
the casket soon. Yeah.

25:26.942 --> 25:27.943
Oh.

25:29.570 --> 25:30.571
[Jinman] Well, then,

25:30.654 --> 25:32.948
I think that's just about everything
I wanted to ask you.

25:34.283 --> 25:37.202
That means I need to speak
with Kim Heeju next.

25:37.286 --> 25:41.957
So are you able to call her here for me,
or do I go somewhere else?

25:42.041 --> 25:43.959
-Kim Heeju?
-Yeah.

25:44.043 --> 25:48.047
Kim Heeju's alibi
hasn't been confirmed yet?

25:48.130 --> 25:49.882
No, we haven't been able
to get a hold of her,

25:49.965 --> 25:51.759
so her alibi is still unclear.

25:52.718 --> 25:54.428
Heeju resigned recently.

25:55.554 --> 25:58.432
She resigned? Why?

25:58.515 --> 26:00.601
She said it was personal.

26:01.518 --> 26:02.519
Oh.

26:04.146 --> 26:05.272
Really?

26:05.355 --> 26:06.565
TEAM LEADER
CHA YUJIN

26:06.648 --> 26:09.985
If you can't reach her, I'll give her
a call and tell her to contact you, okay?

26:10.069 --> 26:12.488
Ah, yeah, if you could do that,
I'd appreciate it.

26:13.572 --> 26:15.449
Apologies for barging in earlier.

26:16.241 --> 26:17.242
Yeah.

26:18.327 --> 26:19.787
Did you buy that yourself?

26:19.870 --> 26:21.038
No, it was a gift.

26:21.622 --> 26:22.623
Gotcha.

26:23.540 --> 26:26.585
Again, apologies for earlier.
Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

26:36.220 --> 26:37.930
[machines beeping]

26:38.013 --> 26:39.515
What's going on with belt two?

26:39.598 --> 26:42.976
[Heeju] It's all the metal decorations
attached to the casket.

26:43.936 --> 26:44.937
Let it go through.

26:46.814 --> 26:49.817
[machine rumbling]

27:06.667 --> 27:10.170
[Yujin] He's gonna ask where you were
when Lee Dokyung had his accident.

27:11.130 --> 27:12.131
Come up with an alibi.

27:17.511 --> 27:18.762
[car horn honks]

27:22.057 --> 27:23.809
Heeju!

27:23.892 --> 27:26.019
[♪ ballad playing over stereo]

27:39.241 --> 27:40.993
[Woogy grunts]

27:44.913 --> 27:46.874
You bought a car?

27:46.957 --> 27:49.501
I bought a new car.
Like it?

27:49.585 --> 27:52.212
The sound is insane.
It's fucking surround sound!

27:52.296 --> 27:55.048
[cheers]

27:56.133 --> 27:59.887
Heeju, you should buy a car or something,
too.

27:59.970 --> 28:01.305
[Woogy grunts]

28:02.806 --> 28:05.225
We already paid the goldsmith one potato.

28:05.309 --> 28:07.895
And I took four out of the 12
as my share.

28:07.978 --> 28:09.479
[Woogy] And that's the rest.

28:09.563 --> 28:13.066
[Woogy] 800 million.

28:14.818 --> 28:16.320
We really did it.

28:17.279 --> 28:18.280
I told you.

28:19.281 --> 28:22.492
Heeju, have you ever seen so much cash?

28:22.576 --> 28:24.369
[Woogy] Couldn't even imagine it!

28:24.453 --> 28:25.746
It's crazy!

28:25.829 --> 28:27.414
We're loaded now!

28:27.497 --> 28:28.999
[Woogy laughing]

28:29.082 --> 28:31.460
[inhales and exhales sharply]

28:31.543 --> 28:35.088
That's one potato down.
Time for us to dig up the next one.

28:35.172 --> 28:38.175
[car engine revving]

28:48.810 --> 28:50.771
[shudders]

28:52.397 --> 28:54.483
Oh, Cheoljung, it's me.

28:54.566 --> 28:57.277
[Mija] How's your head feeling?
Are you okay?

28:57.361 --> 28:59.988
I can't believe Sunok lost
her temper like that.

29:00.072 --> 29:01.365
Let me see.

29:02.491 --> 29:04.117
Good thing it isn't worse, right?

29:04.201 --> 29:07.496
[Mija] Sunok came back
to her senses after she hurt you.

29:07.579 --> 29:09.581
She called the police
and turned herself in.

29:10.248 --> 29:12.125
I told you,
Sunok didn't do it.

29:12.209 --> 29:13.460
[Mija] What do you mean?

29:13.543 --> 29:15.963
She already told me everything.

29:16.046 --> 29:18.215
[blade scraping]

29:18.298 --> 29:19.633
You'll drop the charges, right?

29:21.093 --> 29:23.011
[Mija] You wouldn't really send her
to jail, would you?

29:25.180 --> 29:27.265
You know she has cancer.

29:27.349 --> 29:28.558
She needs a hospital.

29:28.642 --> 29:30.894
She wouldn't make it in a cold jail cell.
STYLE
::cue()

29:30.978 --> 29:33.146
I beg you.
She is your wife.

29:33.230 --> 29:34.523
[scoffs]

29:35.357 --> 29:36.566
My wife?

29:37.609 --> 29:39.695
That bitch was stealing my money.

29:39.778 --> 29:42.072
And I doubt she'd care
if I was killed.

29:42.155 --> 29:44.199
[knife scraping]

29:44.282 --> 29:50.539
About that. Uh, she said she's planning
on returning it all to you.

29:50.622 --> 29:52.040
[Mija] So if it's about the money,
don't worry bec-

29:52.124 --> 29:53.250
Who said?

29:53.333 --> 29:55.669
Who else? Sunok!

29:56.837 --> 29:58.422
It's Heeju, huh?

30:00.257 --> 30:01.883
Ah, no.

30:02.801 --> 30:05.053
Why would you-Sunok, of course.

30:05.137 --> 30:07.514
[Mija] She said she hasn't spent any
of the money yet.

30:08.223 --> 30:10.600
I haven't seen Heeju in over five years.

30:10.684 --> 30:13.353
Why are you suddenly asking about her?

30:13.437 --> 30:16.857
[Cheoljung] Tell Heeju to bring
the money to me herself.

30:18.025 --> 30:19.026
Got it?

30:21.945 --> 30:24.948
Or I'll throw her in
the slammer with her aunt.

30:26.450 --> 30:28.744
[gasping]

30:28.827 --> 30:31.830
[blade scraping]

30:33.206 --> 30:36.293
[cell phone vibrates]

30:37.252 --> 30:39.838
[Mija] Heeju!
This is bad. We're fucked.

30:39.921 --> 30:41.715
That bastard must have seen you.

30:41.798 --> 30:44.009
He says you have to bring him
the money yourself

30:44.092 --> 30:45.427
or he'll report you to the police!

30:45.510 --> 30:47.429
You mean that asshole's still alive?

30:47.512 --> 30:48.889
[Mija] Yes, he's still alive!

30:48.972 --> 30:51.683
He got a few stitches but he survived
and now the bastard's awake.

30:51.767 --> 30:54.019
And apparently he's filing
a police report.

30:54.102 --> 30:55.479
I tried to convince him it wasn't you.

30:55.562 --> 30:57.272
-I really tried.
-[Heeju] It's fine, Auntie.

30:58.607 --> 31:00.567
-[Heeju] I'll take care of it.
-What are you gonna do?

31:00.650 --> 31:02.235
Are you gonna go in there
and meet him face-to-face?

31:02.319 --> 31:03.737
Or are you gonna turn yourself in
to the police?

31:03.820 --> 31:06.823
Oh, it's not like your life
isn't fucked up enough already.

31:06.907 --> 31:11.078
[Mija] Honestly, why is everyone
so hell-bent on screwing themselves over?

31:11.161 --> 31:12.162
Shit!

31:12.871 --> 31:13.872
[cell phone hangs up]

31:16.541 --> 31:17.709
[Heeju exhales sharply]

31:19.044 --> 31:21.213
What happened? Something wrong?

31:22.089 --> 31:24.007
Who's the asshole?

31:29.679 --> 31:31.348
Heeju.

31:31.431 --> 31:32.849
We're partners now, aren't we?

31:32.933 --> 31:35.268
Huh? We're supposed to talk to each other.

31:35.352 --> 31:37.145
Your business is my business.

31:39.606 --> 31:41.191
[Heeju] Do you actually believe that?

31:42.776 --> 31:43.944
That my business is yours?

31:44.820 --> 31:46.947
Of course.
Think about it.

31:48.323 --> 31:53.036
If somethin' happens to you,
it'll screw up our business, hmm?

31:53.120 --> 31:56.498
We only sold one potato.
There's plenty more to do.

31:56.581 --> 31:57.749
[Woogy] I need you for that.

32:04.214 --> 32:05.590
-[scream]
-[groans]

32:05.674 --> 32:07.134
[thuds]
[breathing erratically]

32:12.389 --> 32:13.640
[exhales sharply]

32:13.723 --> 32:15.475
[Woogy] How come you won't just tell me?

32:15.559 --> 32:17.310
I mean, who is it?

32:19.020 --> 32:20.689
[Heeju exhales sharply]

32:21.815 --> 32:22.983
[Woogy] You gonna answer?
STYLE
::cue()

32:27.529 --> 32:28.613
[car alarm beeps]

32:35.620 --> 32:36.621
[seat belt buckles]

32:38.415 --> 32:41.418
[car engine turns over]

32:46.798 --> 32:49.801
[car engine turns over]

32:51.386 --> 32:53.180
[tires squeak]

32:56.850 --> 32:59.853
[♪ suspenseful music]

33:40.310 --> 33:41.311
[car alarm beeps]

33:45.815 --> 33:48.360
[groaning]

33:54.950 --> 33:56.701
[Jinman] Shit.

33:57.994 --> 33:59.120
[exhales sharply]

33:59.204 --> 34:01.289
Pretty damn thorough.

34:01.373 --> 34:02.290
NO DATA

34:02.374 --> 34:03.583
[Jinman] She erased everything.

34:06.044 --> 34:09.714
JEIL WORKSHOP

34:09.798 --> 34:12.801
[blowtorch roaring]

34:28.024 --> 34:29.109
[exhales sharply]

34:29.192 --> 34:32.946
[Woogy] So, uh,
about the situation with your uncle.

34:34.114 --> 34:35.323
I thought about what you told me.

34:37.075 --> 34:38.076
Two options here.

34:38.159 --> 34:42.372
First, give the bastard more money
than he asked for.

34:42.455 --> 34:45.333
Then make him sign something
saying he'll never tell anyone.

34:45.417 --> 34:46.876
Well, that's the first option, anyway.

34:48.586 --> 34:49.629
[exhales sharply]

34:51.631 --> 34:53.216
What's the second option?

34:55.135 --> 34:56.136
[exhales]

34:56.928 --> 34:59.681
I mean, I don't think you'll like it even
if I tell you,

34:59.764 --> 35:01.683
because you're, like,
conscientious and all.

35:02.559 --> 35:03.602
[exhales]
STYLE
::cue()

35:05.061 --> 35:06.146
[smacks lips]

35:08.857 --> 35:10.692
-[exhales]
-[Woogy] Don't worry.

35:10.775 --> 35:12.527
You wouldn't have to do it yourself.

35:12.611 --> 35:15.697
I'll do it for you.
And I'll clean it up, too.

35:19.242 --> 35:20.994
Have you killed people before?

35:23.079 --> 35:24.122
Well, I mean...

35:25.457 --> 35:28.418
...for money, yeah.
I'll do anything for money.

35:29.586 --> 35:30.670
For how much?

35:30.754 --> 35:32.422
[inhales sharply]

35:32.505 --> 35:35.383
Well, a one-kilo gold bar.

35:35.467 --> 35:37.135
[Heeju exhales]

35:38.887 --> 35:41.765
What about my aunt?
Is she trapped in jail?

35:41.848 --> 35:45.602
I mean, if we-
if we get rid of him, then...

35:46.895 --> 35:48.772
...she'd be released
'cause there's no real case.

35:48.855 --> 35:49.981
Oh, wait.

35:50.523 --> 35:52.275
Maybe she'd still have
to serve a year or two.

35:52.359 --> 35:53.360
[Hoonseok clears throat]

35:55.695 --> 35:57.030
How about this one?

35:57.113 --> 35:58.448
[Hoonseok] This batch turned out great.

35:59.616 --> 36:01.409
The bars are super smooth.

36:01.493 --> 36:03.328
-Nice and shiny.
-[Woogy grunts]

36:03.411 --> 36:04.746
[Woogy exhales]

36:04.829 --> 36:06.790
[Woogy] Looks like you're getting better
and better each time.

36:06.873 --> 36:08.041
[Woogy chuckles]

36:08.124 --> 36:10.168
[Hoonseok chuckles]

36:10.251 --> 36:11.252
[Woogy] Okay, back to work.

36:11.336 --> 36:12.462
We're talking here.

36:13.380 --> 36:14.381
[Hoonseok] Ah.

36:17.676 --> 36:18.677
[Woogy exhales]

36:25.558 --> 36:27.060
The first option is good.

36:30.814 --> 36:33.233
Option one, then.
Not my money.

36:33.316 --> 36:35.902
[Woogy inhales and exhales]

36:37.862 --> 36:39.823
[keyboard clacking]

36:45.954 --> 36:48.957
[♪ tense music]

36:52.252 --> 36:54.462
JINGOGAE THREE-WAY INTERSECTION

36:54.546 --> 36:57.215
[mouse wheel scrolling]

36:58.341 --> 36:59.676
[Jinman] Looks like she was lying.

37:01.052 --> 37:02.053
Just watching a movie?

37:03.346 --> 37:05.640
Now I got you, lady.

37:08.935 --> 37:10.186
CHA YUJIN

37:10.270 --> 37:12.605
[groans]

37:13.815 --> 37:15.358
[Gyeongsu yawns]

37:15.442 --> 37:17.569
-[Jinman] Gyeongsu.
-Yeah?

37:17.652 --> 37:18.737
[Jinman] I'm exhausted.

37:18.820 --> 37:20.613
-[Gyeongsu] Well you've been working hard.
-[groans]

37:20.697 --> 37:23.450
Oh, yeah.
That woman who hit her husband.

37:24.534 --> 37:25.577
Was it attempted murder?

37:25.660 --> 37:27.287
-Oh, Yeo Sunok?
-[Jinman] Yeah.

37:27.370 --> 37:28.955
Where's she at?

37:29.038 --> 37:30.290
She's in the holding cell.

37:30.373 --> 37:31.833
-[Jinman exhales sharply]
-Why?

37:31.916 --> 37:34.586
What's up with you?
Why are you still working so late?

37:34.669 --> 37:36.713
The-the report isn't done yet.

37:38.173 --> 37:39.215
Get back to it.

37:39.299 --> 37:40.592
[Gyeongsu] Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

37:47.599 --> 37:49.934
-[Male Officer] Sir.
-[Jinman] Yeah.

37:50.018 --> 37:53.605
Listen, I have a few questions
for the detainee.

37:53.688 --> 37:56.024
Do you mind giving me the room just
for ten minutes?

37:57.150 --> 37:58.318
[Male Officer] Of course, sir.

37:58.401 --> 38:01.404
[keys jangling]

38:02.363 --> 38:03.698
[lock clangs]

38:03.782 --> 38:05.700
[door creaking]

38:05.784 --> 38:06.785
[Jinman] Thanks.

38:09.412 --> 38:10.914
-Come back in 10.
-[Male Officer] Yes, sir.

38:10.997 --> 38:12.749
[Jinman] 'Kay.

38:16.377 --> 38:17.545
[exhales]

38:24.552 --> 38:26.846
[Jinman groaning and exhaling]

38:31.935 --> 38:32.936
[scoffs]

38:35.146 --> 38:37.690
[both scoffing]

38:37.774 --> 38:39.651
[laughing]

38:39.734 --> 38:40.735
Hey.

38:41.694 --> 38:44.572
Of all the places we could have met, huh?

38:44.656 --> 38:46.199
[inhales and exhales sharply]

38:49.911 --> 38:51.704
[puffing]

39:02.715 --> 39:04.843
[Jinman] Did you beat your husband
with a golf club?

39:05.510 --> 39:07.720
Mm-hmm.

39:07.804 --> 39:09.305
Why?

39:10.682 --> 39:12.433
Just wanted the bastard dead.

39:13.643 --> 39:16.855
[Jinman] Ah, that temper of yours.

39:16.938 --> 39:20.191
If you say things like that in court,
they'll put you right in prison.

39:21.109 --> 39:22.443
I don't care.

39:23.611 --> 39:24.904
So what if they do?

39:26.239 --> 39:28.449
It wouldn't even make that much
of a difference.

39:29.450 --> 39:32.078
Your husband says it was 'cause of money.

39:32.161 --> 39:33.413
[scoffs]

39:33.496 --> 39:34.914
Well, that's part of it, too.

39:41.546 --> 39:43.715
So this morning I overheard something.

39:43.798 --> 39:46.759
You have cancer?
That true?

39:47.927 --> 39:50.013
Seems like it.

39:50.096 --> 39:51.764
Then stop smoking, Sunok.

39:52.932 --> 39:54.267
Uh, here.

39:54.350 --> 39:55.935
[Sunok exhales sharply]

40:04.152 --> 40:05.486
You mean to settle?

40:06.487 --> 40:08.406
No, I'll just go to prison, I think.

40:09.741 --> 40:11.200
It sounds easier.

40:11.284 --> 40:12.827
[door opens]

40:16.623 --> 40:18.958
[Jinman] I'll go talk to your husband in
a couple of days.

40:19.959 --> 40:21.002
Don't bother.

40:21.711 --> 40:23.171
It doesn't matter.

40:28.676 --> 40:30.720
[door creaks and clangs]

40:30.803 --> 40:33.890
[keys jangling]

40:36.643 --> 40:37.644
[door closes]

40:44.025 --> 40:45.652
[glass bottle shatters]
[fist slams on table]

40:45.735 --> 40:48.112
If you order a drink then shut up
and fucking drink it

40:48.196 --> 40:49.822
-like a good little boy. You hear that?
-Oh, fuck you!

40:49.906 --> 40:52.909
[all screaming]

40:54.452 --> 40:56.329
[sirens blaring]

40:56.412 --> 40:57.580
[tires screech]

40:57.664 --> 40:59.290
[distant shouting]

41:02.251 --> 41:05.004
GWIBIN COFFEE SHOP

41:05.088 --> 41:06.798
[Man] The police, police!

41:07.757 --> 41:09.676
[Police Partner] We're the police!
Break it up!

41:09.759 --> 41:10.885
[Police Partner] Hey, hey!

41:10.969 --> 41:12.011
[Woman] Don't push me!

41:12.095 --> 41:14.973
[Police Partner] Come on!
That's enough. That's enough.

41:15.056 --> 41:16.015
Hey, hey.

41:16.099 --> 41:17.433
Just calm down.

41:17.517 --> 41:19.519
-[Police Partner] Hey!
-[Woman] Leave her alone.

41:19.602 --> 41:22.105
[all shouting]

41:22.188 --> 41:23.564
-Put me down!
-[Woman] There he goes!

41:31.280 --> 41:32.323
[exhales sharply]

41:33.992 --> 41:35.201
Give me a light?

41:39.122 --> 41:40.206
[lighter flicking]

41:42.000 --> 41:43.001
[lighter flicking]

41:43.084 --> 41:44.627
[flame sizzles]
STYLE
::cue()

41:47.797 --> 41:48.715
[gasps]

41:48.798 --> 41:50.675
[Sunok] How come your hands are so pretty?

41:52.468 --> 41:53.886
You play piano, officer?

41:53.970 --> 41:55.054
Uh, no, ma'am.

41:58.307 --> 41:59.475
[exhales]

42:02.520 --> 42:04.272
[lighter flicking]

42:04.355 --> 42:05.356
Guess it's true.

42:06.691 --> 42:08.151
Men in uniform are pretty sexy.

42:08.234 --> 42:10.403
[coughing]

42:12.655 --> 42:16.451
[giggling]

42:50.485 --> 42:51.778
Heeju!

42:52.612 --> 42:53.696
[Cheoljung] You're here.

42:54.447 --> 42:56.866
I was wondering when you'd show up.

43:00.828 --> 43:02.121
Just look at you!

43:03.664 --> 43:05.583
All grown up.
A real woman now.

43:06.793 --> 43:11.047
I'm only here-I'm here to-
to return the money Auntie took from you.

43:11.130 --> 43:13.382
What she stole?

43:14.383 --> 43:15.384
Sure.

43:16.302 --> 43:18.471
How much money?

43:19.972 --> 43:21.224
100 million.

43:26.979 --> 43:29.524
And how are you planning on returning it?

43:30.233 --> 43:32.235
[Heeju] I can send it
to your bank account.

43:32.318 --> 43:34.904
Or if you want I can give it
to you in cash.

43:36.030 --> 43:37.657
[Cheoljung] Really?

43:37.740 --> 43:39.492
Hmm.

43:40.368 --> 43:42.370
Well, I want it back in cash.

43:42.453 --> 43:43.746
[Heeju] Yes.

43:43.830 --> 43:45.456
But before that...

43:46.499 --> 43:48.876
...you have to drop
the charges against auntie.

43:50.711 --> 43:52.713
Sure, no problem.

43:52.797 --> 43:54.841
Then the three of us can live together.

43:54.924 --> 43:57.218
We're family after all, aren't we?

43:57.301 --> 43:58.386
No.

44:01.472 --> 44:03.182
Auntie isn't doing very well.

44:04.267 --> 44:05.268
It's cancer.

44:06.060 --> 44:07.603
She might not live long.

44:09.272 --> 44:10.982
So I want her to get treated.

44:11.607 --> 44:13.234
In a hospital.

44:13.317 --> 44:16.863
While there's still time
and she can live comfortably.

44:16.946 --> 44:18.865
[Heeju] I'll stay by her side
while she's there.

44:19.448 --> 44:20.658
But uncle...

44:21.617 --> 44:23.911
...you're going to leave town
and not come back.

44:25.913 --> 44:27.707
Why would I?

44:29.083 --> 44:30.543
See, the thing is,

44:30.626 --> 44:32.920
the house and the shop are here,
so where would I go?

44:33.004 --> 44:34.589
[Heeju] You can sell the pawnshop to me.

44:36.215 --> 44:37.800
I've already looked into it.

44:37.884 --> 44:41.679
I know all about the loans and that
the shop is being used as collateral.

44:41.762 --> 44:44.932
I'll take over your debts,
pay you the rest...

44:45.766 --> 44:47.226
...and I'll even pay in cash.

44:48.644 --> 44:49.854
How much?

44:51.689 --> 44:53.733
How much do you want for it?

44:56.360 --> 45:00.031
I won't sell it at market price. Hm.

45:01.282 --> 45:03.659
Maybe for a billion won,
I'd let you have it.

45:03.743 --> 45:05.244
Okay.

45:08.206 --> 45:09.624
Seriously?

45:09.707 --> 45:12.543
You got that kinda cash?
That much?

45:14.629 --> 45:15.630
Yeah.

45:16.839 --> 45:17.924
Is that so?

45:18.883 --> 45:20.968
For that kind of money...

45:21.886 --> 45:23.971
[Heeju] Come to the pawnshop
by 10:00 o'clock tonight.

45:25.014 --> 45:27.058
I'll have the contract
and the money ready for you.

45:27.141 --> 45:28.142
But first...

45:29.810 --> 45:31.437
...you need to drop the charges.

45:32.230 --> 45:33.481
Or the deal's off.

45:34.398 --> 45:35.566
Mm-hmm.

45:36.525 --> 45:37.568
Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

45:52.083 --> 45:53.292
[exhales sharply]

45:53.834 --> 45:54.961
[grunts]

45:59.465 --> 46:00.800
How did it go?

46:00.883 --> 46:03.386
One billion to take his debt
and the store.

46:03.469 --> 46:05.179
Ah, shit, that's crazy.

46:06.222 --> 46:09.850
A billion won for that crumbling,
one-story building? Really?

46:09.934 --> 46:12.186
-Drop me off at Yangpo Airport.
-[Woogy] Why?

46:12.895 --> 46:14.814
I'm a bit short on cash.

46:14.897 --> 46:16.107
How much more do you need?

46:16.857 --> 46:19.193
I can have it ready
for you in just two days.

46:19.277 --> 46:23.155
No, it has to be today.
I want to get my aunt out quickly.

46:23.239 --> 46:24.657
[exhales sharply]

46:24.740 --> 46:26.659
We're fucked. Shit.

46:28.494 --> 46:30.913
Let me just lend it to you, okay?

46:34.583 --> 46:35.960
CONFIRMATION OF SEVERANCE PAY RECEIPT
KIM HEEJU

46:36.043 --> 46:39.213
[announcement chiming over speakers]

46:39.297 --> 46:42.049
[Female Announcer] We will now
begin boarding.

46:46.053 --> 46:48.597
I'll tell them to send it out immediately,
since it seems urgent.

46:48.681 --> 46:51.142
Oh, thank you very much.
I appreciate it, Ms. Cha.

46:51.225 --> 46:53.311
Where are you living nowadays, Heeju?

46:53.394 --> 46:54.312
What?

46:55.229 --> 46:57.523
I decided to take a look at your resume.

46:57.606 --> 47:00.192
Your address and listed family are fake.

47:01.944 --> 47:03.654
[Yujin] What exactly are you hiding?

47:05.698 --> 47:08.242
-I'm staying with my aunt.
-[Yujin] Oh, really?

47:08.326 --> 47:10.286
And where does your aunt live?

47:11.329 --> 47:12.371
In Jeongsan.

47:13.205 --> 47:14.540
Jeongsan?

47:15.124 --> 47:18.627
[Jinman] Have you been to Jeongsan,
by any chance, recently?

47:18.711 --> 47:20.504
-No.
-[Jinman] Okay.

47:20.588 --> 47:22.214
You haven't then.

47:22.298 --> 47:24.133
-Why are you asking?
-[Jinman inhales sharply]

47:24.633 --> 47:26.385
[Jinman] Seems the smuggling
accomplice went

47:26.469 --> 47:28.596
to Jeongsan with the casket.

47:30.139 --> 47:31.140
[inhales]

47:32.933 --> 47:34.143
There's no way.

47:35.186 --> 47:36.979
You're the accomplice.

47:37.980 --> 47:39.065
What?

47:39.940 --> 47:41.650
Have you given your alibi?

47:41.734 --> 47:44.570
Uh, no, not yet.

47:44.653 --> 47:45.654
Okay, well...

47:46.864 --> 47:49.450
...give the detective a call.
Do that first.

47:49.533 --> 47:51.327
[Yujin] It might be best
to get ahead of it.

47:51.410 --> 47:54.330
Just don't mention you're in Jeongsan,
because the thing is,

47:54.413 --> 47:56.874
the police know that the van carrying
the casket went there.

47:56.957 --> 47:59.585
[Yujin] Heeju, they're gonna find you.

47:59.668 --> 48:01.087
It's only a matter of time.

48:04.090 --> 48:07.343
I'm not sure I know
what you're talking about.

48:07.426 --> 48:08.677
[exhales]

48:10.096 --> 48:11.138
Okay.

48:12.223 --> 48:14.642
Can't blame you, I guess.

48:14.725 --> 48:15.893
Lee Dokyung is a bad guy.

48:17.144 --> 48:18.521
[Yujin] Didn't I ever tell you?

48:18.604 --> 48:19.605
No?

48:20.731 --> 48:22.942
Lee Dokyung and I dated for a while.

48:24.235 --> 48:25.444
[Yujin] Not anymore, though.

48:26.904 --> 48:29.240
I was on National Route 6 that day, too.

48:29.990 --> 48:32.868
He asked me to help him move the casket.

48:32.952 --> 48:35.454
Obviously, I refused to help out.

48:35.538 --> 48:37.456
You were clearly too blinded
by love, though.

48:38.416 --> 48:39.417
[Yujin] It made you foolish.

48:40.918 --> 48:44.338
He has as lover
in every location he flies to
STYLE
::cue()

48:44.422 --> 48:46.132
I bet you didn't know that.

48:46.215 --> 48:50.094
China, Hong Kong, Vietnam, Japan.

48:52.179 --> 48:54.181
[Yujin] There are probably more here, too,
that we don't know about.

48:55.474 --> 48:58.060
Do you think he actually loves
all those women?

48:59.228 --> 49:00.312
Or are you telling yourself,

49:00.396 --> 49:05.568
those relationships are all fake,
and you're the only one he truly loves?

49:08.571 --> 49:09.989
[exhales]

49:10.823 --> 49:14.577
I seriously don't know what you mean
by any of these things.

49:16.996 --> 49:18.998
Ms. Cha, why are you telling me all this?

49:19.915 --> 49:20.958
I'm trying to help you.

49:22.168 --> 49:24.503
We're suspects.

49:24.587 --> 49:27.089
As long as you're in the clear,
then I'm in the clear.

49:28.257 --> 49:32.595
[Yujin] Lee Dokyung is just using you
and you keep letting him.

49:33.929 --> 49:35.097
He's not worth it.

49:36.390 --> 49:38.726
I wish you had just run off
with the casket yourself.

49:38.809 --> 49:40.144
That would have been better.

49:41.228 --> 49:44.273
[Yujin] But could you really hold out
on your own with the casket,

49:44.356 --> 49:46.025
until Lee Dokyung gets outta jail?

49:52.490 --> 49:53.949
Remember this, Heeju.

49:54.909 --> 49:56.869
I'm the only person on your side now.

49:56.952 --> 50:00.706
If something happens,
you should call me immediately.

50:00.789 --> 50:02.082
[Yujin] I can help you out.

50:19.892 --> 50:22.394
[inhales and exhales deeply]

50:38.452 --> 50:40.871
What? Are they not gonna pay you?

50:41.914 --> 50:43.582
Want me to take care of it?

50:43.666 --> 50:45.000
No.

50:46.335 --> 50:47.670
[cell phone vibrates]

50:47.753 --> 50:48.754
[phone clicks]

50:48.837 --> 50:49.964
[exhales]

50:53.050 --> 50:54.093
THIS IS DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN.
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU SEE THIS MESSAGE.

50:54.176 --> 50:55.177
I'M CONTACTING YOU FOR A WITNESS
INTERVIEW. I HAVE A FEW THINGS TO ASK YOU.

50:56.220 --> 50:58.138
-Ah, shit.
-[Woogy] What?

50:58.222 --> 51:00.182
Who is it?

51:00.266 --> 51:02.351
It's the police.

51:03.269 --> 51:04.270
What?

51:05.187 --> 51:06.188
What do they want?

51:07.231 --> 51:09.567
Shit, did that fucker
Han Cheoljung report you?

51:09.650 --> 51:12.528
No, the detective looking for the casket.

51:12.611 --> 51:15.656
He suspects I helped Lee Dokyung.

51:16.657 --> 51:19.952
Sounds like the police also know that
the van went to Jeongsan that day.

51:25.583 --> 51:27.626
Ah, shit.

51:27.710 --> 51:29.545
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
Hold on.

51:29.628 --> 51:30.629
[Woogy] What are you doing?

51:31.589 --> 51:33.882
If I don't call him,
he'll suspect me more.

51:34.800 --> 51:36.969
[exhales]

51:37.052 --> 51:38.137
Hold on a sec.
STYLE
::cue()

51:46.895 --> 51:48.314
Put it on speaker, okay?

51:48.397 --> 51:51.066
[cell phone trilling]

51:52.484 --> 51:54.695
[Jinman] This is Detective Kim Jinman

51:54.778 --> 51:55.988
-of the Jeongsan Police.
-Uh...

51:56.530 --> 51:57.531
...yes, hello.

51:57.615 --> 52:00.534
You called because I used
to work at Yango Airport?

52:00.618 --> 52:02.077
-This is Kim Heeju.
-Kim Jinman of Jeongsan?

52:02.161 --> 52:04.288
[Jinman] Oh, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

52:04.371 --> 52:07.875
Seems like Cha Yujin finally managed
to get a hold of you, then.

52:07.958 --> 52:10.711
Anyway, well, I tried calling a bunch.

52:10.794 --> 52:13.505
Then I stopped by your house
but you weren't there either.

52:13.589 --> 52:17.885
I even went to Yangpo Airport
and they told me you left the company.

52:19.303 --> 52:20.846
Is that right?
You no longer work there?

52:20.929 --> 52:26.894
Uh, yeah, I've just been busy
with personal stuff so...

52:27.978 --> 52:29.730
[Jinman] No worries.
Nothing major.

52:30.731 --> 52:32.566
Just need to know where you were the day
of Lee Dokyung's accident.

52:34.360 --> 52:36.737
The date was September fourth,
if you recall.

52:38.447 --> 52:41.533
[Heeju] Uh, after I got off work...

52:42.660 --> 52:47.498
...I remember I drove up to-
to Gangneung for the evening.

52:47.581 --> 52:50.042
[Jinman] Gangneung?
And why go there?

52:50.125 --> 52:51.877
You came all the way back
to work the next day.

52:52.920 --> 52:57.424
[Heeju] Yeah, I just wanted
to clear my head,

52:57.508 --> 52:59.718
so I went shopping
and then went to see a movie.

52:59.802 --> 53:01.178
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

53:03.013 --> 53:05.974
A movie, huh? On your own?

53:08.060 --> 53:09.269
Yeah.

53:09.353 --> 53:10.813
[Jinman] I see.

53:10.896 --> 53:12.272
You don't have a car, right?

53:13.065 --> 53:14.191
No.

53:14.274 --> 53:15.567
[Jinman] Okay, I got it.

53:15.651 --> 53:16.902
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

53:16.985 --> 53:18.153
I'll be able to check
the rest on my end here.

53:18.237 --> 53:20.280
All right, well,
thanks for calling.

53:21.323 --> 53:22.408
Ooh.

53:22.491 --> 53:23.992
Ah, shit!

53:24.076 --> 53:26.036
Kim Jinman's with the company.

53:26.120 --> 53:29.248
-He's a detective.
-Yeah, well, obviously.

53:29.331 --> 53:31.083
But he's a detective who works with us.

53:33.627 --> 53:35.504
Hey, Detective.
Doing okay?

53:37.464 --> 53:39.675
[Woogy] Jeongsan Police,
Investigations Division, right?

53:40.592 --> 53:43.303
That means it's not the fucking cops.
It's Yes Money chasing you.

53:43.387 --> 53:44.888
They want to find their casket.

53:46.265 --> 53:48.851
[Woogy] Ah, we're really fucked now.

53:49.601 --> 53:51.228
[exhales sharply]

53:53.105 --> 53:54.273
-Oh.
-Sir.

53:54.356 --> 53:56.024
Uh, looks like the charges
are being dropped.

53:56.525 --> 53:58.318
-O-open it. I need to talk to her.
-Yes, sir.

53:58.402 --> 53:59.236
Thanks.

53:59.319 --> 54:02.030
[keys rattling]

54:02.114 --> 54:03.782
[Jinman] Ms. Yeo Sunok.

54:03.866 --> 54:05.159
[door creaking]

54:05.242 --> 54:06.535
Yeo Sunok.

54:07.411 --> 54:09.663
What? Miss Yeo Sunok.

54:11.039 --> 54:13.751
Hey, Yeo Sunok.

54:15.836 --> 54:18.172
Sunok. Sunok! Wake up!

54:18.255 --> 54:19.798
Hey, help me out here!

54:19.882 --> 54:21.049
[Male Officer] Yes, sir.

54:21.133 --> 54:22.509
[grunts]

54:22.593 --> 54:23.927
[Jinman] Okay, call 911.

54:24.011 --> 54:26.013
-Call them right now!
-[Male Officer] Yes, sir.

54:26.096 --> 54:28.974
[distant sirens blaring]

54:37.816 --> 54:40.944
[gasping]

54:41.028 --> 54:43.739
[Mija whimpers]

54:43.822 --> 54:45.699
[Mija] Sunok. Sunok, wake up.
Come on.

54:46.700 --> 54:47.701
[Mija gasps]

54:47.784 --> 54:49.495
What's wrong with her?

54:50.120 --> 54:51.830
[Mija] Doc-doctor!

54:51.914 --> 54:53.749
[gasps]
No!

54:53.832 --> 54:55.125
Sunok, no!

54:55.751 --> 54:58.212
Sunok, please, open your eyes!

54:58.295 --> 54:59.546
[Mija crying]
[Mija] Sunok!

54:59.630 --> 55:01.089
Please!

55:01.173 --> 55:02.966
[crying]

55:04.384 --> 55:07.054
[Mija] They said she got blood
in her lungs and went into shock.

55:07.137 --> 55:08.472
Oh, so stupid.

55:08.555 --> 55:11.225
She could have asked them
to take her to the hospital.

55:11.308 --> 55:14.645
But instead she just sat there suffering
with a hole in her lung.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.146
Like she wanted to die.

55:17.064 --> 55:18.899
So, what did you say to your uncle?

55:19.733 --> 55:22.361
He dropped the charges.
How did you manage that?

55:22.444 --> 55:23.946
[inhales deeply]

55:24.029 --> 55:26.865
Will you please do me a favor
and stay with her tonight?

55:26.949 --> 55:27.824
I'll be there tomorrow.

55:27.908 --> 55:29.660
[inhales]

55:29.743 --> 55:31.203
[groans]

55:31.286 --> 55:33.789
Tonight? It's Friday, though.

55:34.373 --> 55:37.543
[grunts]
I'm supposed to be working tonight.

55:38.794 --> 55:39.920
[exhales]

55:40.003 --> 55:42.923
I-I'll pay you a million won
for your trouble.

55:44.424 --> 55:45.842
[Mija] Okay, okay.

55:45.926 --> 55:47.761
I'm sorry, auntie.
Thank you.

55:48.804 --> 55:52.891
[phone beeps]
[inhales and exhales sharply]

55:55.686 --> 55:56.687
Heeju.

56:01.733 --> 56:03.068
Let's take a sec to think about it.

56:03.151 --> 56:04.319
About what?

56:06.196 --> 56:09.032
[Woogy] About shutting Han Cheoljung up
with hush money.

56:09.116 --> 56:10.158
How can you be sure?

56:10.993 --> 56:12.786
That asshole could still
rat you out after.

56:14.830 --> 56:16.248
The second he gives your name
to the police,

56:16.331 --> 56:17.874
Detective Kim will find out, too.

56:18.750 --> 56:21.128
That means he'll know without
a doubt you went to Jeongsan.

56:24.006 --> 56:25.007
[exhales sharply]

56:25.090 --> 56:27.426
But he did get my aunt out
like he promised.

56:27.509 --> 56:28.635
Exactly.

56:29.553 --> 56:31.471
So you don't have
to worry about her anymore.
STYLE
::cue()

56:40.522 --> 56:42.065
Didn't you say you wanted him dead?

56:43.859 --> 56:44.860
[Woogy] Heeju.

56:44.943 --> 56:46.695
You think it'll end here?

56:47.154 --> 56:48.196
Not a chance.

56:48.280 --> 56:50.574
[Woogy] I know assholes
like him too damn well.

56:50.657 --> 56:53.535
He'll keep coming back,
asking for money again and again.

56:57.372 --> 56:59.708
[Woogy] As long as you and your aunt
are still here,

56:59.791 --> 57:00.876
he'll never leave you alone.

57:02.210 --> 57:05.088
Why put yourself in such
a dangerous situation?

57:05.172 --> 57:06.965
And if Detective Kim catches you...

57:08.050 --> 57:09.760
...then it'll all be over, Heeju.

57:09.843 --> 57:11.720
The gold bars.
Everything.

57:13.305 --> 57:20.312
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

57:34.660 --> 57:36.995
Haengbok Pawnshop, huh?

57:40.957 --> 57:43.043
[door creaks]

57:43.126 --> 57:44.628
[Cheoljung] Heeju!

57:58.975 --> 58:00.060
Read it over.

58:13.657 --> 58:15.992
So, the money.
Where is it?

58:16.076 --> 58:18.328
I wanna see it myself first.

58:18.412 --> 58:19.913
[exhales]

58:21.998 --> 58:23.834
[grunting]

58:25.335 --> 58:27.003
[Heeju grunts]

58:29.923 --> 58:31.550
[zipper unzips]

58:39.182 --> 58:40.100
[Cheoljung gasping]

58:40.183 --> 58:43.061
I didn't believe you!
What the...

58:43.603 --> 58:46.398
...what the hell have you been doing
all these years, Heeju?

58:46.481 --> 58:50.193
[Cheoljung] I mean, how could you
possibly have this kind of money?

58:54.531 --> 58:55.699
Sign the contract.

58:55.782 --> 58:58.118
Uh, okay.
Yeah, sure.

59:03.123 --> 59:04.416
[zipper zipping]

59:05.459 --> 59:06.793
[exhales]

59:07.461 --> 59:09.796
You know I can't do it, Heeju.

59:13.341 --> 59:16.511
[Cheoljung] Let's stop
and think this over again, okay?

59:16.595 --> 59:19.139
[Cheoljung] Who cares
who owns the pawnshop?

59:19.222 --> 59:20.390
That doesn't matter.

59:21.308 --> 59:23.059
Family is all that matters.

59:23.143 --> 59:26.813
You and me, your aunt,
we should all live together.

59:29.149 --> 59:30.525
Sign the contract.

59:30.609 --> 59:32.569
I'm not telling you again.

59:32.986 --> 59:34.946
[Cheoljun] The whole drive here,

59:35.030 --> 59:36.948
I put a lotta thought into this.

59:37.866 --> 59:39.117
[inhales and exhales sharply]

59:39.201 --> 59:40.327
Your poor aunt.

59:40.410 --> 59:43.455
[Cheoljung] She has cancer
and not much time to live.

59:43.538 --> 59:46.750
I just think while she's alive,
she'd be happier if we were all together.

59:46.833 --> 59:48.293
We're supposed to be family.

59:48.376 --> 59:49.628
[scoffs]

59:49.711 --> 59:52.005
[chuckles]

59:52.964 --> 59:55.008
-Family?
-[Cheoljung] If we weren't family,

59:55.091 --> 59:58.011
I would've reported you
to the police right away, ya know?

59:58.094 --> 01:00:00.680
[Cheoljung] You swung that club at me.

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:03.266
I saw your face as clear as day.

01:00:04.643 --> 01:00:08.605
[Cheoljung] Or would you rather I go
to the police right now

01:00:08.688 --> 01:00:10.982
and let 'em know it was you?

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:15.111
[Heeju grunts]

01:00:15.987 --> 01:00:18.990
What should I spend all this money on?
Pay off the loan?

01:00:19.074 --> 01:00:22.118
Well, seeing as it is our store,
let's do that.

01:00:22.202 --> 01:00:25.622
Oh, sweetie, being on your own
was so hard wasn't it?

01:00:32.045 --> 01:00:35.131
No. No! No! No!

01:00:35.215 --> 01:00:37.050
-[grunting]
-Ah, shit.

01:00:37.133 --> 01:00:39.511
[grunting]

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:40.929
[Cheoljung grunts]

01:00:41.012 --> 01:00:42.556
[slaps]
[Heeju wails]

01:00:42.639 --> 01:00:44.391
Ah, you little shit.

01:00:44.474 --> 01:00:46.601
[Heeju groaning]

01:00:48.103 --> 01:00:50.772
[groaning]

01:00:50.856 --> 01:00:52.858
[Cheoljung] Don't even think
about leaving.

01:00:52.941 --> 01:00:56.069
Just stay here
and look after the pawnshop.

01:00:56.152 --> 01:01:00.115
[Cheoljung] While your aunt dies.

01:01:00.198 --> 01:01:01.658
[snickers]

01:01:01.741 --> 01:01:06.329
[coughing]

01:01:06.413 --> 01:01:09.416
[Heeju gasping]

01:01:14.546 --> 01:01:15.547
Goodbye.

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:19.551
[groaning and gasping]

01:01:20.594 --> 01:01:21.970
[Heeju] Woogy!

01:01:22.971 --> 01:01:24.890
[door creaking]

01:01:27.434 --> 01:01:28.560
[door lock clicks]

01:01:28.643 --> 01:01:31.062
Bastard, who are you?

01:01:31.146 --> 01:01:34.107
[groaning]

01:01:34.190 --> 01:01:36.735
Evil son of a bitch.
STYLE
::cue()

01:01:42.574 --> 01:01:44.117
Should I do it?

01:01:44.200 --> 01:01:47.203
[clock ticking echoes]

01:01:50.999 --> 01:01:52.000
Yeah.

01:01:54.794 --> 01:01:55.879
Do it.

01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:57.547
[both grunting]
[blade slices]

01:01:57.631 --> 01:02:00.550
[both shouting]

01:02:00.634 --> 01:02:03.637
[pained gasping]

01:02:07.515 --> 01:02:10.143
[both grunting]
[blade slicing]

01:02:19.152 --> 01:02:22.072
[blade piercing]

01:02:22.155 --> 01:02:25.158
[gagging and sputtering]

01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:31.039
[blood squelching]

01:02:31.122 --> 01:02:33.833
[Woogy breathing heavily]

01:02:36.670 --> 01:02:39.673
[♪ dramatic music]

01:02:47.973 --> 01:02:49.307
[blade clatters]

01:02:50.016 --> 01:02:53.061
[both breathing heavily]

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:18.962
[♪ music continues]
